      "id": "05",
      "source_unit": "float-math",
      "title": "Floor Division with Floats",
      "sidebar_tag": "//",
      "description": [
        "<p>Read two floats, one per line, and print <code>a // b</code> using the",
        "floor division operator <code>//</code>. With floats, the result still",
        "rounds down to a whole number &mdash; but stays a <strong>float</strong>",
        "instead of becoming an int.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "7.5",
        "2.0",
        "3.0</pre>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "# TODO: read two floats, then print a // b"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "7.5",
            "2.0"
          ],
          "expected": "3.0"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "10.0",
            "3.0"
          ],
          "expected": "3.0"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "9.5",
            "4.0"
          ],
          "expected": "2.0"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "23.0",
            "5.0"
          ],
          "expected": "4.0"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "100.0",
            "7.0"
          ],
          "expected": "14.0"
        }
